{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Draw near, please, to me.</b> To tell them the matter of recognition in a whisper, so that others would not hear. Another interpretation: they are able to draw near, for they are many, but he cannot draw near, for if he approaches this one he moves away from that one; and his intention was not for his own honor but for their honor. Rashi: he showed them that he is circumcised, and one need not worry that perhaps he is Ishmaelite — for there are many circumcised ones, but Ishmaelites are not circumcised until after thirteen years, and on account of intercourse there is no periah (uncovering); but the children of Israel who are circumcised when they are young — the periah is clearly visible. And even though the Egyptians were circumcised, as Rashi explained on 'whatever he says to you, you shall do' — that was on account of the distress of famine; but he is rich, so if so he would not have been circumcised if he were not a Jew. Another interpretation: the tribes did not know in Egypt that the Egyptians are circumcised, and therefore they could recognize Joseph by his circumcision."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:39.806558558Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}